.\" The manual page for Viddl.  roff rather than Markdown because it has to
.\" survive `man`, and because a package recipe looks for a file in this shape
.\" rather than for a paragraph on a web page.
.TH VIDDL 1 "2026-10-29" "Viddl 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viddl \- download a video or a song by pasting a link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viddl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B viddl
downloads a video, or just its audio, from any of the hundreds of sites
.B yt-dlp
supports.  Run with no arguments it opens a full\-screen terminal app: paste a
link, pick a quality from the list it fetches, and the file lands in your
Downloads folder with its path printed when it is done.  Mouse and keyboard
both work.
.PP
The app looks after its own dependencies.  The first download fetches
.B yt-dlp
(about 3 MB) into its own folder, or uses one already installed, preferring the
newest copy it can find.
.B ffmpeg
is only fetched when a job needs it \- a conversion to MP3, M4A, Opus, FLAC or
WAV, or a quality whose video and audio have to be merged \- and it says how
large that download is before starting it.
.PP
There is no server and no account, and nothing leaves the machine except the
download itself.  Links handed over by the browser extension are only ever
filled into the link box; nothing is looked up or saved until a person presses
Enter and then chooses a quality.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Everyday use
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-uri " URL"
A
.B viddl://
link handed over by the browser extension.
.TP
.B \-\-audio
Start on the audio options: the site's own file, or MP3, M4A, Opus, FLAC or WAV.
.TP
.BI \-\-list\-qualities " URL"
Print the qualities a link offers and exit, without downloading anything.
.TP
.BI \-\-download\-dir " DIR"
Save downloads here for this run instead of the Downloads folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-extras " LIST"
Also add subtitles, details (title, channel, date and chapters) or a cover
image.  The list is comma\-separated:
.IR subs ,
.IR details ,
.IR cover ,
or
.I all
for the three of them.
.TP
.BI \-\-cookies\-from\-browser " BROWSER"
Let the download use the cookies the browser already has, for a site that asks
you to sign in:
.IR chrome ,
.IR firefox ,
.IR edge ,
.IR brave ,
.IR safari ,
or
.I auto
for whichever is installed.
.TP
.B \-\-download\-archive
Remember what has been downloaded, in Viddl's own folder, and skip videos
already saved.  Re\-running a playlist then takes only the videos it has not
fetched yet.
.TP
.B \-\-live\-from\-start
For a live stream, record it from its beginning instead of from the moment you
start.  Not every site can serve the part it has already played.
.SS Downloading without the screen
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Download a line at a time instead of opening the full\-screen app, in plain
ASCII, for scripts and older consoles.
.TP
.B \-\-accessible
Like
.BR \-\-plain ,
but no line is ever written over and the end rings the bell, for a screen
reader.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
With
.BR \-\-plain ,
print only the saved path.  Progress and notes are left out; failures still go
to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " QUALITY"
With
.BR \-\-plain :
a height such as
.I 720
or
.IR 1080 ,
.IR best ,
or an audio format:
.IR audio ,
.IR mp3 ,
.IR m4a ,
.IR opus ,
.IR flac ,
.IR wav ,
or a preset such as
.IR mp3\-192 .
.TP
.B \-\-yes
With
.BR \-\-plain :
download without asking first, for scripts.
.TP
.B \-\-playlist
With
.BR \-\-plain :
download every video of a playlist, one after another, instead of only the
first.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With
.B \-\-doctor
or
.BR \-\-list\-qualities :
print one JSON object instead of sentences, for scripts.
.SS A slow connection, a busy one, or a proxy
.TP
.BI \-\-limit\-rate " SPEED"
Download no faster than this, so other things on the connection still work:
.IR 500K ,
.IR 2M ,
or a number of bytes per second.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " ADDRESS"
Send downloads through a proxy:
.IR http://host:port ,
.IR socks5://host:port ,
or an address that carries a sign\-in.
.TP
.BI \-\-concurrent\-fragments " N"
How many pieces of one video to fetch at once, from 1 to 32 (the default is 4).
Lower it when a site or a proxy complains.
.TP
.BI \-\-throttled\-rate " SPEED"
Give up on a source that stays slower than this and try another:
.I 100K
or
.IR 1M .
.SS What the screen looks like
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " THEME"
The colours the app draws in:
.IR dark ,
.IR light ,
.IR high\-contrast ,
or
.I auto
to follow the terminal's background.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LANG"
The language the explanations are written in:
.I en
or
.IR es .
The default is whichever language the computer is set to.
.SS Remembered settings
.TP
.BI \-\-set " SETTING VALUE"
Remember a preference in Viddl's settings file.  The settings are
.IR download\-dir ,
.IR quality ,
.IR archive ,
.I theme
and
.IR notify .
.TP
.BI \-\-unset " SETTING"
Forget a remembered preference, so the built\-in default applies again.
.SS Tools and versions
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Show where Viddl keeps its files, where downloads go, whether the engine and
.B ffmpeg
are ready, and which environment variables are in effect.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Fetch the newest video engine.  This is the fix for a link that used to work and
now does not, and it says which version it moved from and to.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-ffmpeg
Fetch the newest
.B ffmpeg
build.  This is the fix when merging or converting fails.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
With
.BR \-\-version :
also print Python, yt\-dlp and ffmpeg, each with where it came from \- the four
numbers a bug report needs, in one block.  It only looks for the helpers, so it
is safe on a machine that has never downloaded anything.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Print a block to paste into a bug report: the version block, the last failure
from the log already redacted, and where the log lives.  Nothing is sent
anywhere.
.SS The browser hand\-off
.TP
.B \-\-register\-protocol
Make
.B viddl://
links open the app.  The browser extension needs this; the installer does it.
.TP
.B \-\-unregister\-protocol
Stop handling
.B viddl://
links.
.TP
.BI \-\-install\-browser\-extension " [BROWSER]"
Copy the bundled extension to a folder you can load:
.I chrome
(also Edge and Brave) or
.IR firefox .
Give no browser to do both.
.TP
.BI \-\-extension\-zip " [BROWSER]"
Write the extension as the zip an add\-on store accepts.
.TP
.B \-\-extension\-path
Print the folder holding the bundled browser extension.
.SS A page in your browser
.TP
.B \-\-web
Open a page on this computer that downloads with the same tools, for when a
browser tab is easier than a terminal.  It listens on 127.0.0.1 only, never on
the network, and every request must carry the random token printed when the page
started.
.SS Being told when it is done
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Say so when a download that took a while finishes: a desktop notification where
there is one, the terminal's bell otherwise.  Very short downloads stay quiet.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Never notify, even when the settings file asks for it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIDDL_HOME
The one folder Viddl owns.  Defaults to
.I ~/.local/share/viddl
on Linux and macOS and
.I %LOCALAPPDATA%/viddl
on Windows.
.TP
.B VIDDL_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Where downloads are saved.  Defaults to the usual Downloads folder.
.TP
.B VIDDL_YTDLP
A particular copy of
.B yt\-dlp
to run, instead of the one Viddl would choose.
.TP
.B VIDDL_FFMPEG
A particular
.B ffmpeg
to run, including one Viddl installed for itself.
.TP
.B VIDDL_YTDLP_ARGS
Extra options for
.BR yt\-dlp .
Options that would write files or run commands are refused rather than passed on.
.TP
.B VIDDL_TIMEOUT
How long to wait for the network, in seconds, before a look\-up is given up on.
.TP
.B VIDDL_ARCHIVE
When set, skip videos already downloaded, as
.B \-\-download\-archive
does.
.TP
.B VIDDL_QUALITY
The quality to use when none is chosen, as
.B \-\-set quality
would remember.
.TP
.B VIDDL_THEME
The colour scheme to draw in, as
.B \-\-set theme
would remember.
.TP
.B VIDDL_NOTIFY
When set to something true, say so when a long download finishes, as
.B \-\-notify
does; set it to false to turn that off again.
.PP
A flag on the command line beats an environment variable, an environment
variable beats the settings file, and the settings file beats the built\-in
default.  A setting that quietly does not apply is worse than no setting, so
.B \-\-doctor
prints which of these are in effect.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/viddl/
Viddl's own folder, private to the account that created it.  It holds:
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/viddl/bin/yt\-dlp
The video engine, if Viddl fetched one.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/viddl/bin/ffmpeg
The copy Viddl installed, if it did.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/viddl/viddl.log
What failed and what the failing tool said.  No run that worked writes a line.
The file rolls over at 256 KB and keeps one older copy.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/viddl/recent.json
The list of what was saved lately, shown by pressing
.I r
in the app.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/viddl/config.toml
The optional settings file.  On Linux and macOS without
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.I ~/.config/viddl/config.toml
is used; on Windows,
.IR %APPDATA%/viddl/config.toml .
The file is written only by
.B \-\-set
and
.BR \-\-unset .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested work succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Something failed.  The reason is on standard error, written for a person rather
than for a log.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the app with a link already loaded:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
viddl 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Download 720p without the screen, for a script:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
viddl \-\-plain \-\-yes \-\-quality 720 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Make an MP3 from a link that needs a sign\-in:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
viddl \-\-plain \-\-yes \-\-quality mp3 \e
      \-\-cookies\-from\-browser firefox 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...'
.fi
.RE
.PP
See whether a link is worth downloading, as JSON:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
viddl \-\-json \-\-list\-qualities 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Collect the numbers a bug report needs:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
viddl \-\-version \-\-verbose
viddl \-\-report
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
and the project's README at https://github.com/0xzntb/video\-downloader for the
screens, the settings and the browser extension.  The engine's own options are
documented at https://github.com/yt\-dlp/yt\-dlp.
.SH BUGS
Report them at https://github.com/0xzntb/video\-downloader/issues, with the
output of
.B viddl \-\-report
pasted in.  Nothing is sent automatically: Viddl has no telemetry, and the
report is only something your own terminal prints.
.SH AUTHOR
Viddl contributors.
